WEBVTT

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:11.333
Okay, before we made a sling using the double fisherman's knot.

00:00:10.583 --> 00:00:13.291
This is a sling that I use.

00:00:12.458 --> 00:00:24.875
It is kind of a longer sling, but I use this for a backing up belay device such as like an ATC, or Traffic Control, or a figure eight.

00:00:23.916 --> 00:00:27.333
I will show you how to use that later.

00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:33.958
But anyway, first thing you need to know about your sling is a way to carry it around that is useful.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.416
A lot of guys will throw it over like so.

00:00:34.458 --> 00:00:36.875
This kind of bothers me just because it is just something that could get stuck.

00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:50.208
What I actually like to do is start at the bottom and kind of fold it in half.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:56.791
I am going to leave enough room because we are going to wrap the other end around this.

00:00:55.958 --> 00:01:07.250
And you just start wrapping like so.

00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:11.125
You just keep going around till you get to the end.

00:01:10.166 --> 00:01:11.416
Then you have this loop on here that is created from the rope that we just wrapped around and pass the loop from the rope that you were wrapping and then you can tighten it up here.

00:01:10.458 --> 00:01:11.583
This gives you a nice little hook or a loop to hook through with a Caribbean or whatnot.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:12.041
It is not the best to store because if you store a rope and you are going to put weight on it, it is not the best idea to have because it starts to break down the fibers.
